Played on the Steam Deck
Finished in: around 9,5 hours

THE GOOD:
+ the graphics are gorgeous!
+ the sound design is top-notch;
+ it's a really solid remake of the original RE3, changing some things which didn't age well, while not interfering too much;
+ the game can really whoop your *** if you're not careful and try to be a hero;
+ the dialogues are still cheesy, but seem more plausible than the ones in the original;
+ the constant fear of being chased by Nemesis can be tiresome, but it feels so satisfying when you finally finally finally defeat him (after faux-defeating him like 5 times);
+ Jill Valentine is much more likable and fleshed-out than in REmake 1;
+ it's nice to see the intertwining story with REmake 2;
+ plenty of stuff to unlock with repeated playthroughs;
+ AMAZING optimisation for the Steam Deck! The game is already set up for the best graphics/performance right out of the box, and it runs smooth as butter while still looking delicious!
+ the gameplay is a nice combination of the old school TPP with the FPP from RE7
+ I actually liked Carlos;

THE BAD:
- how many times can Nemesis die and come back up?
- after playing REmake 2, this one smacks you in the face with it's completely different approach... in REmake 2 you have to be careful, strategic and constantly think where to head next. This game is the opposite; it is pure action upon action and more action;
- the puzzles are super-simple and easy to figure out (but that has been my gripe with all Resy games);

THE UGLY:
~nothing

YOU'LL LIKE IT IF:
you like old school survival-horror, you like RE (duh), you like zombies and improbable sci-fi plots

This is a good action game, but not a good Resident Evil. This game is so short that it could be easily sold as a Resident Evil 2 Remake expansion pack. If you don't own Resident Evil 2 Remake, buy that instead.

[u]Pros[/u]
+ Good action game;
+ Excelent modding community.

[u]Cons[/u]
- You can beat the campaign in under 2 hours;
- The game is extremely easy and don't offer you any good challenges, you can even use the infinite weapons on Inferno difficulty mode and get an S Rank;
- There are no puzzles at all;
- There is several parts of the original game missing, the story has been completely redone;
- You don't get any choices when Nemesis is after you like in the original game;
- It only took me about 30 hours to get all the achievements with no rush, you can do it with even less time than that;
- There are no extras, no new scenarios, no mercenaries mode, nothing, only the main campaign
- There is only a single extra costume for Jill, if you want to get one more for Jill and Carlos, you need to buy the DLC;
- No DLCs, only the 2 garbage costumes that should have been for free.

Very fun to be honest, I just wish it told you that theres....3 "hardest" difficulties ;-;
