It makes me so sad how Resident Evil 3 (2020) was so unfaithful to what was supposed to be its source material, the old Resident Evil 3: Nemesis (1999). When you look at Resident Evil 2 (2019) you can see that they've tried many wild and different things, but it still felt like a remake made by people that loved and respected the original. I can't say that they had the same respect for this game... :'(

I know that Capcom is calling these games a "reimagining" and not a remake, but for those that played RE3 Nemesis, it's easy to see how much that made it great has been completely removed. And we bearly got anything back in return. That's not the fair treatment that a mainline Resident Evil game deserves. RE2 definitely had some shortcomings, but many people and I were willing to forgive them because we had such a good experience with a game that tried to be faithful to the original.

Right now it must be obvious for you that I'm a big fanboy of the original... and you're not wrong. RE3 Nemesis is a game that I love very much and I consider it to be the best RE game in the entire series. But it's important to note that my expectations for this remake were increased exponentially because of o RE2, they set the bar high, so it was only fair to expect RE3 to be just as good, if not better. Can you blame me?

So, from here on out I'll just list my pros and cons. I'll try to be as fair and impartial as possible at this point. I consider some of these to be minor spoilers, so I'll be hiding them under the spoiler tag.

[b]PROS:[/b]
[list]
    [*]Jill, Carlos, Mikhail, and Tyrell are much better written and more fleshed out this time around. [spoiler]I think this new Carlos is so much better that he almost steals the spotlight from Jill as the main character[/spoiler];
    [*]The new character and monster designs are great (Nemesis is an exception for me);
    [*]The gameplay and graphics are just as amazing as they were in RE2R (an exception is zombies dismemberment, they're gone for some reason);
    [*]The dodge mechanic is a welcome addition to keep the game more fast-paced and more faithful to the original;
    [*]The [spoiler]flamethrower[/spoiler] Nemesis boss fight was pretty nice;
    [*]The hospital area is way better compared to the original.
[/list]

[b]CONS:[/b]
[list]
    [*]The old "Live Selection" is gone, any form of multiple path choices were not implemented;
    [*]The items and enemy placement only change if you play on the most challenging and brutal difficulties: Nightmare and Inferno. Every difficulty below that will always be the same;
    [*]This game is very linear with some minimal backtracking. For some players this could be good news, but this is not how the original was, so I'll leave is as a con;
    [*]Puzzles are basically a foreign concept to this game, don't expect to find them like in RE2 ([spoiler]if you consider that railway rerouting as a puzzle, you'll get a whopping total of TWO puzzles! I don't think people consider finding locker and safe combinations as puzzles either[/spoiler]);
    [*]The background music was present this time, but some of the tracks are so quiet that I couldn't even hear them properly without headphones (no way to increase BGM volume more than the default 100%);
    [*][spoiler]The Uptown was completely on rails, no way to explore while you were there, neither a way to go back[/spoiler];
    [*]the Downtown area felt super short;
    [*]Most of Nemesis chases ([spoiler]excluding the ones that are quick-time events and cutscenes[/spoiler]) were very linear, run from point A to point B or die ([spoiler]he can't be put down for more than 10 seconds or so[/spoiler]);
    [*]The Drain Deimos (the flea-like creatures) were only used in a single area, [spoiler]and it was very short too[/spoiler];
    [*]The old Nemesis' phase 2 (multiple tentacles) is not present in any way;
    [*][spoiler]No RPD as Jill[/spoiler];
    [*][spoiler]The Clock Tower interior[/spoiler] was removed;
    [*][spoiler]The Raccoon Park[/spoiler] was removed;
    [*][spoiler]The graveyard[/spoiler] was removed;
    [*][spoiler]Grave Diggers (giant worms)[/spoiler] were removed;
    [*]No crows nor spiders (not a surprise considering RE2R scrapped them);
    [*]The incentives to re-play are minimal. You have three choices: (1) Achievement hunting; (2) Get a better score on a certain difficulty; (3) Complete challenges to unlock some helpful/cheaty items;
    [*]If you choose not to use those cheaty items that I mentioned, you get no extra rewards when finishing the game without them;
    [*]There's only ONE unlockable costume, the other existing two were pre-order bonuses.
[/list]

For those that like to see a score, I think this game deserves no nome then a: [b]6/10[/b].

Got this as a gift from my friend and maybe it would get better ratings and more players if it was at least 10$ cheaper. It’s a bundle of two games: RE3 and RE Resistance (an equivalent of Dead by Daylight).  

Pros: 
+ the graphics and the sound are amazing;
+ I love how Capcom integrated some visual effects from RE7, it makes RE3 even more atmospheric;
+ dodge mechanics and animation.

Cons:
- it’s toooooooo short, I wish there were more quests and puzzles, and I wish they were more difficult; 
- the story is good but not great, it’s quite linear, it lacks plot twists; 
- beating Nemesis was interesting… for the first two times. After that, he becomes too easy to dodge and predictable.

Overall, it’s more like a good continuation of RE2 which impressed me more at first. However, I really enjoy this game. It helps me to relieve stress and I really feel happy playing it. Going to play it again and again. So this one is my favorite game so far cuz for me its pros matter much more than cons.

